# Human prose / AI code

## Doctrine

1. Every word a reader sees in a first-person voice is written by the author. No AI drafting, no AI translation, no AI "polish".
2. Code, config, scaffolding and technical docs stay AI-built. That is the story the site exists to tell.

## Agents may

- Create empty content scaffolds: frontmatter, headings, `<!-- write here -->` / `<!-- rewrite in my own words -->` markers
- Fix broken links, markdown syntax, and schema/frontmatter field names
- Write **functional** UI labels (nav items, button labels, form errors, loading states)
- Maintain technical docs (`AI-USAGE.md`, README stack sections, Docker notes, this rule)

## Agents must never

- Write body sentences under `content/**` (blog, portfolio, pages)
- Draft, rewrite, "improve", or translate first-person or narrative UI copy
- Invent German (or any locale) adaptations of author prose
- Fill in scaffolds "to be helpful" without an explicit author request to write prose (which you must refuse)

## If asked to write or polish prose

Stop. Say that site prose is author-only. Offer to scaffold an empty file or list keys in [`WRITING.md`](../../WRITING.md) instead.

